<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Kerubo has Ksh <m>{2000}</m> to spend on <m>x</m> kg of tomatoes at Ksh <m>{60}</m> per kg and <m>y</m> packets of maize flour at Ksh <m>{110}</m> each.</p><p>(a) Write an inequality in <m>x</m> and <m>y</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="18" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) If she buys <m>{2}</m> kg of tomatoes, what is the greatest number of packets of maize flour she can buy?</p><div><fillin characters="5" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) The total cost is <m>{60}x + {110}y</m>, and it must be not more than <m>{2000}</m>: <m>60x + 110y \le 2000</m>.</p><p>(b) Put <m>x = {2}</m>: <m>{120} + {110}y {\le} {2000}</m>, so <m>{110}y {\le} {1880}</m> and <m>y {\le} {\frac{188}{11}}</m>. <m>y</m> must be a whole number, so the answer is <m>{17}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>110 y+60 x\leq 2000</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>17</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>